{
  "note": "Workspace configs both loaders must refuse. Python forbids extra keys on every config block (config.py's ConfigDict(extra='forbid')); the TypeScript loader mirrors those tables in server/src/config.ts. A config that loads in one language and not the other is the bug this fixture exists to catch, so the spellings here are Python's canonical snake_case ones \u2014 a camelCase alias TypeScript would otherwise accept for free is just as unportable as a typo. A case may name an `error`: a phrase both loaders' refusals must contain.",
